• For 32 GB+ RAM: 1G–1.5G is reasonable.

• If your machine starts swapping (disk thrashing),
  the compression will be MUCH slower than just
  using a smaller dictionary in the first place.

RECOMMENDATION
──────────────
Pick the largest dictionary that fits comfortably
in ~60-70% of your FREE RAM. Check with:
  free -h
